---- MODULE hello ----
\* HardyRTOS scheduling model for hello
\* Generated by HardyScript RT module

EXTENDS Integers, Sequences, FiniteSets, TLC

CONSTANTS
    Tasks,        \* Set of task IDs
    Priorities,   \* Priority levels
    TickBound     \* Max ticks to explore

VARIABLES
    state,        \* state[t] \in {"ready", "running", "blocked"}
    priority,     \* priority[t]
    deadline,     \* deadline[t] (ticks)
    wcet,         \* wcet[t] (ticks)
    clock,        \* current tick
    running,      \* currently running task
    missed        \* set of tasks that missed deadline

TypeInvariant ==
    /\ state \in [Tasks -> {"ready", "running", "blocked"}]
    /\ priority \in [Tasks -> Priorities]
    /\ running \in Tasks
    /\ clock \in 0..TickBound

Init ==
    /\ state = [t \in Tasks |-> "ready"]
    /\ clock = 0
    /\ missed = {}
    /\ running = CHOOSE t \in Tasks : TRUE

\* Scheduler picks highest priority ready task
Schedule ==
    LET best == CHOOSE t \in Tasks :
        /\ state[t] = "ready"
        /\ \A s \in Tasks : state[s] = "ready" => priority[t] <= priority[s]
    IN running' = best

\* Safety property: no deadline miss
NoDeadlineMiss == missed = {}

\* Liveness: every task eventually runs
Fairness == \A t \in Tasks : <>(running = t)

\* Task parameters (from HardyScript @periodic annotations):

==== End MODULE hello ====
